{
    "pr_body": "The test `testDataStreams_autoFollowAfterDataStreamCreated` in `AutoFollowIT` sometimes fails on CI where a backing index of a datastream cannot be followed because it already exists (see #72062).\r\n\r\nWhile looking at the test I noticed that : \r\n- `AutoFollowIT` extends `ESCCRRestTestCase` which does not wipe clusters between tests;\r\n- multiple tests use the same auto-follow pattern `logs-*`;\r\n- tests do not always clean up indices/datastreams/auto-follow patterns on all test clusters, specially when the test fails and leaves existing resources  that can conflict with subsequent tests.\r\n\r\nI have the feeling that #72062 is caused by conflicting auto-follow patterns but I wasn't able to reproduce the issue. Therefore I am opening this pull request that adds clean up logic for tests in `try...finally` blocks. It also changes the `logs-*` patterns for data streams tests so that they are not conflicting anymore.\r\n\r\nCloses #72062",
    "original_commit_id": "988ca7380fb03a10d7ece3ba00e7088aef2a045f",
